# Vue 3

- Composition API + `<script setup>` for all new components.
- `ref` for primitives, `reactive` for objects — but prefer `ref` everywhere for consistency. Reactivity is easier to reason about with one primitive.
- Do not destructure a `reactive()` object outside a `toRefs()` call; you'll lose reactivity.
- Composables (`useX`) are the Vue equivalent of hooks. Keep them pure, no side effects at import.
- Provide/inject is context. Use it for truly global values (theme, i18n), not to skip 2 levels of props.
- `defineProps` + `withDefaults` with TS. No PropTypes-style runtime objects.
- Emit events via `defineEmits`. Never mutate a prop from a child.
- Pinia > Vuex. Do not add Vuex to a new project.
- Template refs are typed via `ref<InstanceType<typeof MyComponent> | null>(null)`.
